      "title": "Setup required \u00b7 select models and a saved bundle",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Reference person in a new scene - Flux.2 Klein Base 4B\n\nChoose a saved Flux.2 bundle in Image RefMod Apply. For the SAME reference photos saved for another family, bake a separate Flux.2 bundle with flux2-vae.safetensors first; family labels do not convert latents. Use the named model, qwen_3_4b encoder and matching VAE in this graph. No edit LoRA is needed for this preset.\n\nThe reference supplies appearance; the prompt describes a new full-body pose, outfit, camera view and environment. The output starts from a separate empty 1024x768 canvas, not from the reference pixels. Change the target width/height AND Flux2Scheduler dimensions together.\n\nThis exact model/sampling path was checked with a saved portrait in full-weight generation. That is a starting example, not a guarantee of exact identity for every person, seed or scene. Inspect facial identity as well as whether the requested composition changed. The bundle is a reusable collection of references; it adds no identity-training capability beyond the underlying model.\n\nSampling: Klein Base 4B, seed 42, Euler, 20-step Flux2Scheduler, CFG 5. Do not substitute distilled Klein or Flux.2 dev without updating their model components and sampling."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Reference person in a new scene - Flux.2 Klein Base 4B\n\nChoose a saved Flux.2 bundle in Image RefMod Apply. For the SAME reference photos saved for another family, bake a separate Flux.2 bundle with flux2-vae.safetensors first; family labels do not convert latents. Use the named model, qwen_3_4b encoder and matching VAE in this graph. No edit LoRA is needed for this preset.\n\nThe reference supplies appearance; the prompt describes a new full-body pose, outfit, camera view and environment. The output starts from a separate empty 1024x768 canvas, not from the reference pixels. Change the target width/height AND Flux2Scheduler dimensions together.\n\nThis exact model/sampling path was checked with a saved portrait in full-weight generation. That is a starting example, not a guarantee of exact identity for every person, seed or scene. Inspect facial identity as well as whether the requested composition changed. The bundle is a reusable collection of references; it adds no identity-training capability beyond the underlying model.\n\nSampling: Klein Base 4B, seed 42, Euler, 20-step Flux2Scheduler, CFG 5. Do not substitute distilled Klein or Flux.2 dev without updating their model components and sampling."
      }
    },
